Z||000000||fierofreek2001||05-22-2001||11:09 PM||||i saw a fiero at carlisle with the front compartment where the spare tire would normally go, carpeted.. is there any pics of this that i can see?  was this professionally done?... i was thinking of putting 2 subs up there , and i thought a carpeted front would look nice<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000001||jaguiler||05-23-2001||12:11 AM||||Freak,<BR>I met you up in Carlise...I am John with the red GT.  I saw the carpeted car...it looked nice.  I think you can do it yourself.  Just go to the store and get "tan" carpet....or "gray.... start with siccors and chop away the basic shape.  then make small slits for the curves.  Use a tacky sray glue (buy it with the carpet...made jsut for that) and glue it....shoudl work fine...I have done this several times with my jeep....<BR>you will be surprised what a good job you can do with some patience....<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||05-23-2001||09:11 AM||||Look mine in photo and previous post bellow. I did it myself. Not to hard but time consuming and back pain. A lot of trial & error to get it right. I did one pice for the center-front trunk wall down all the way to the firewall. Then separate pieces for each fender. I bought the carpet at Autozone (rubbermade). I did my rear trunk the same way.<BR>Forum topic: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006441.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006441.html</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pe752ae15fd6dff0ba010fb49fee29c45/fea7b7f1.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
